  "code_review": {
    "walk_forward": "features.build computes every game's features for a (season, week) batch before updating ratings with that batch's results; Elo and opponent-adjusted EPA state are therefore pre-week. pipeline._train_mask admits only played games from earlier seasons/weeks. pipeline.add_ensemble_walk_forward refits stacks on those earlier out-of-sample component predictions. models.kalman.run_kf also predicts a whole week before applying that week's results.",
    "kalman_tuning": "kalman.tune explicitly slices season < before_season before likelihood optimisation. A regression test guards that cutoff. However models/kf_params.json has no per-season training-window metadata; the checked-in values cannot be independently proven to have been generated by that code path.",
    "lightgbm": "The walk-forward component path uses _train_mask and refits before each season/week. The repository contains no reproducible hyperparameter/feature-selection history, so it cannot prove that manual model selection was not influenced by later seasons.",
    "point_in_time_risk": "Historical schedule fields home_qb_id/away_qb_id and temp/wind feed QB-rate/change and LightGBM features. The repository does not retain point-in-time snapshots or availability timestamps for those fields. Actual starter identity and observed game weather may differ from what was knowable at forecast time. This is a potential availability leakage risk, not a demonstrated result-leakage bug; its impact is not quantified in PR2 because doing so requires point-in-time inputs and a separate controlled re-evaluation.",
    "processed_data_provenance": "contract.data_snapshot hashes data/raw/*.parquet, while feature construction also reads data/processed/team_games.parquet and qb_games.parquet. Those processed files are derived from raw inputs but are not directly hashed in the prediction provenance; stale derived caches remain a reproducibility risk.",
    "injury_lag": "The feature builder uses Out/Doubtful counts from week t-1 or t-2, not the current week. This avoids direct same-week injury-report leakage, although source publication timestamps are not retained in the historical feature cache."
  },
  "conclusions": [
    "MARKET clearly outperforms MODEL_ONLY on accuracy, Brier and log loss; paired stratified block CIs stay well above zero under 1-, 2- and 4-week block lengths.",
    "Point estimates slightly favour MARKET over ENSEMBLE, but the difference is tiny and block-length sensitive (the 95% CI crosses zero on Brier under 1-, 2- and 4-week blocks and on log loss under 1-week blocks); there is no robust separation between MARKET and ENSEMBLE, and no evidence that ENSEMBLE improves upon MARKET.",
    "The high-confidence (75%+) overconfidence hypothesis reproduces for MODEL_ONLY's own favourites (+4.35 pp, 95% CI strictly above zero across 1-, 2- and 4-week blocks), whereas ENSEMBLE's own 75%+ segment is +0.74 pp with CIs spanning zero under all block lengths.",
    "Constrained ensemble weight variants (ens_cap1, ens_pool) do not separate from the published ensemble under any block length (all CIs cross zero); no retuning in PR2."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Primary intervals use 2-week blocks stratified by season (72 blocks across 8 seasons, never crossing season boundaries) with 1-week and 4-week sensitivity checks; intervals are not adjusted for multiple comparisons.",
    "Historical QB identity and weather features lack point-in-time availability timestamps.",
    "Stored Kalman parameters and manual LightGBM/model-selection history lack per-season provenance.",
    "Processed team_games and qb_games caches are derived inputs but are not directly hashed.",
    "No model weights or hyperparameters were retuned; frozen snapshots were not rewritten; no Odds API calls were made."
  ]
}
